The '''demographics of [[Burawa]]''' encompass the population, ethnicity, language, religion, and other statistical characteristics of the people of [[Burawa]]. As of 2026, Burawa has a population of approximately 127.5 million, making it the most populous country in [[Southwestern Kaftia]] and the fifth-largest economy on [[Adonia]].

Burawa's demographic history has been shaped by three defining periods: the [[Burawi Domestic War]] (1932–1935), during which the [[Act of Self-Determination]] and political upheaval caused mass emigration; the [[Great Adonian War]] (1935–1948), which inflicted significant population losses through military casualties and displacement; and the [[Burawi baby boom]] (1962–1985), during which the population more than doubled. Since the 1990s, sustained immigration has driven continued growth, and approximately 22% of the country's residents are non-citizens.

== Population ==

