=== Urbanisation ===

Burawa is a highly urbanised country, with approximately 87% of the population residing in urban areas. The urban population is divided between the eight [[metropolitan administrations of Burawa|metropolitan administrations]], which account for 58% of the total population (74 million persons), and the 86 independent urban administrations, which account for a further 28% (36 million persons). The remaining 13% of the population (16 million persons) lives in rural administrations.

{| class="wikitable"
! Settlement type !! Number !! Population !! Percentage
