The proportion of the population identifying as mixed ethnicity has risen steadily since the mid-twentieth century, driven by intermarriage in the metropolitan regions. The mixed-ethnicity share is highest in [[Iskhal Megalopolis]] (12%), [[Kankadadka-Samara Megalopolis|Kankadadka-Samara]] (10%), and [[Lake Haro]] (10%), and lowest in the rural regions of [[Central Burawa]] (2%) and [[Dhulsarren]] (3%).

The [[Iracwi people]] are the indigenous population of the [[Buran River Valley]], [[Kwalib]], and [[Kushish]] highlands, constituting the largest non-Burawi indigenous group. The [[Dakari people|Dakari]] and [[Tukulor people|Tukulor]] are concentrated in the northern [[Dimar]] region and around the margins of the [[Great Kaftian Lake]].

The [[Darasian people|Darasian]] and [[Baliscano people|Baliscano]] communities originate from the socialist exchange programmes of the 1950s–1970s, when citizens of [[Daras]] and [[Balisca]] settled in Burawa under diplomatic agreements. These communities are concentrated in the [[Kankadadka-Samara Megalopolis]], near the institutions of government and the military academies that hosted the exchange programmes.

The [[Enfolian people|Enfolian]] community is the largest immigrant-origin group, reflecting the sustained immigration from [[Enfolo]] since the 1990s. Enfolian workers are concentrated in the [[Lake Haro]] and [[Buran River Valley]] industrial regions.

The [[HBCD]] (Historical Burawi Colony Born Diaspora) is a demographic category comprising descendants of persons born in former Burawi colonies who do not identify with the indigenous populations of those territories and retain little indigenous ancestry. The HBCD population is distributed across the metropolitan areas and constitutes a distinct social group within Burawi society.

The [[Jarani people|Jarani]] community originates from [[Jarin]] and is present in small numbers across the metropolitan regions. The [[Ayori people|Ayori]], from neighbouring [[Ayorin]], are concentrated in [[Eastern Burawa]] and the [[Dimar]] region. A small but established [[Shansi people|Shansi]] community, originating from the [[Shansi]] region of [[Fosia]], is present in the major metropolitan areas.

