== Language ==

[[Burawi language|Burawi]] is the sole official language of Burawa and serves as the lingua franca across all ethnic groups. The language is spoken by approximately 190 million persons across Burawa and neighbouring countries including [[Fayeha]], [[Kijura]], [[Galwa]], [[Wolonia]], and [[Kwalib]]. Regional dialects exist, particularly in the northern and western regions, but standard Burawi is the language of government, education, media, and commerce.

