== Education ==

=== Structure ===

Education in Burawa is compulsory until the age of 18. The system is divided into three stages: primary education, secondary education, and tertiary education. Upon completion of secondary education at age 18, all Burawi citizens are required to complete the [[Burawi Work Programme]], a period of national service lasting between one and four years depending on the track selected. The Work Programme encompasses military service, civil service, healthcare assistance, infrastructure development, and other public-interest placements.

Each urban administration maintains at least one college or minor university. The following ten institutions are regarded as the principal centres of higher education in Burawa.

